        "title": "Add managed realtime capability to Sites hosting",
        "summary": "The Sites subsystem in the common package now supports managed room realtime through a new `FreebuffRealtime` Durable Object and a `sites_prepare_realtime` tool that generates local helper files without requiring Cloudflare credentials. The deployment manifest accepts a realtime boolean flag that is only valid when true, and the `sites_prepare_next` tool now includes a realtime parameter to enable the platform binding for Next.js projects. Five other changes are included: stdin streaming for preparation programs to avoid Windows command-line limits, version pins moved to a dedicated module, guidance updates for realtime, private file filtering for the realtime directory, and Durable Object validation in Worker publishing.",
        "significance": "major",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "New files `common/src/sites/realtime-prepare.ts` and `common/src/sites/realtime-worker.ts` define the `FreebuffRealtime` Durable Object and local helper generation. `common/src/sites/tools.ts` adds the `sites_prepare_realtime` tool spec and extends `sites_prepare_next` with a realtime parameter. `common/src/sites/local-files.ts` adds `realtime: z.literal(true).optional()` to the deployment manifest schema.",
        "userVisible": true,
        "confidence": "medium",
